codex
The macro inspection confirms the classification: `type()` is DATA_MODELED by `MultiVersionJavaPacket::to_id`, whose `#[java_packet(CONSTANT)]` expansion reads the generated `PacketId::to_id` table. I also confirmed the packet classes are wired to live send paths (camera, equipment, passengers, respawn, inventory, experience, links, etc.); there is no missing `type()` implementation to add without inventing a parallel API. I’m doing one focused protocol regression test so this run ships Rust and verifies the modeled replacement against vanilla’s `type()` contract.
