The comparison confirms every listed `type()` lead is generated by `#[java_packet]`/`#[packet]`, so those are `DATA_MODELED`, not missing Rust methods. `CocoaBlock.createBlockStateDefinition` is also represented by generated `Block::COCOA.states` and `CocoaLikeProperties`; its runtime hooks already cover placement, growth, survival, neighbor updates, and bonemeal. I found one concrete parity defect while reading the listed packet: vanilla’s store-cookie codec caps payloads at 5120 bytes, while both Rust store-cookie models currently write arbitrary lengths. I’m wiring that existing encoder path and adding a boundary test.
